# catalog/lane-run-inputs.d/mr-red.rw — the files one
# `bin/staff/mr-red.sh work <payload>` run writes (BH-9532, C0 of #9532). A
# write-back may carry these only. The ro snapshot is these plus mr-red.ro.
# In C0 no lever has a _work function, so a run writes nothing but its log.
#
# NOT CARRIED (machine-local caches and logs, safe to lose):
#   state/mr-red/checks/* (the check-run cache of bin/staff/mr-red-collect.d/
#   10-drafts.sh; the tick writes it on the hub, never a work run),
#   state/gh-budget/*, state/flags-cache/*.
# Secrets and locks are never carried: env/*, locks/*.
# logs/staff-mr-red.log rides back as the lane log (.lri/log-append).
